[{"url": "https://terracon.com/insight/navigating-broadband-permitting/", "content": "Navigating Broadband Permitting Challenges\n\nPermitting is one of the most time-consuming aspects of fiber deployment. Terracon's team works to streamline the permitting process for clients, coordinating with local municipalities, utilities, and right-of-way authorities to minimize delays and keep projects on schedule.\n\nOur approach includes early engagement with permitting authorities, thorough documentation, and proactive communication to reduce the likelihood of permit kickbacks and delays. Terracon's experience across multiple states and municipalities enables the team to anticipate common permitting challenges and address them before they cause project delays.\n\nWith BEAD funding driving unprecedented broadband deployment activity, permitting timelines are under increasing pressure as municipalities deal with higher volumes of permit applications.\n\nKey factors contributing to permitting delays:\n- Incomplete or inaccurate construction drawings\n- Utility conflicts not identified early\n- ROW documentation gaps\n- Insufficient as-built records from prior projects"}]
